    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0773" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2859</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-02T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1570. Department’s circular September 20, 6 p.m. Foreign Office replies that
                    Mexican Government has instructed its diplomatic agents <pb facs="0774" n="700"
                        xml:id="pg700"/> to report as to the true situation in Russia. As soon as
                    these reports are received and if the case merits, Mexican Government will
                    consider what attitude it should adopt in evidence of its sympathy for the
                    Russian people.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
